{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]An expert in the law stood up [Ab]to test him in the [Eb]crowd
Teacher, which is the greatest command[Ab]ment, he asked a[Bb]loud
[Cm]Jesus did not hesitate, his [Ab]answer came out [Eb]plain
He gave them back the ancient words they'd [Ab]heard and heard a[Bb]gain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You shall [Eb]love the [Bb]Lord your [Cm]God with all your [Ab]heart
With [Eb]all your [Bb]soul, and with [Cm]all your [Ab]mind
This is the [Eb]great and first command[Bb]ment
And the [Cm]second is [Ab]like it
[Eb]You shall love your [Bb]neighbor as your[Eb]self
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Ab] | [Bbsus4] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Ab] [Eb/G] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Love him when you're rising [Ab]and love him when you [Eb]rest
Love him with your thinking and the [Ab]heart within your [Bb]chest
And [Cm]the one who lives beside you and the [Ab]stranger at your [Bb]door
[Eb]Love them like you love yourself, [Ab]that's what the law [Bb]is for
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Ab] | [Bb7sus4] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Ab] [Eb/G] | [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]On these [Ab]two command[Eb]ments hang the [Bb]whole law and the [Cm]prophets
With [Ab]all [Eb]your [Bb]heart
With [Ab]all [Eb]your [Bb]soul
With [Ab]all [Eb]your [Bb]mind
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You shall [Eb]love your [Bb]neighbor [Cm]as your[Ab]self
With [Eb]all your [Bb]heart
{end_of_verse}

